# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# There was no such file until the image started building the website, and that
# is what made one necessary: the site stage copies apps/website wholesale, and
# without these lines it would copy its node_modules and a dist left behind by
# a local `npm run build` -- the second of which would then shadow the fresh
# build with whatever happened to be on the machine.
#
# Everything here is either generated or irrelevant to a server image. The Go
# stage copies three named paths and is unaffected; this only shrinks what has
# to be sent to the daemon before it starts.

**/node_modules
apps/website/dist
apps/studio/frontend/dist
apps/studio/frontend/bindings
apps/charted/dist

bin
.task
.tmp-verify
apps/studio/build/linux/appimage/build

.git
.github
.claude
